     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Wanting it settled before the family visit and evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for 1000 mg. That dose is 5 times the maximum, and I'd expect it to cause serious harm in a 70 kg adult with normal organ function.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, sertraline 50 mg PO once daily, or 100 mg if the patient is already established on it. That would be in place before evening rounds.\n- **Add a note for the team.** The order can say the dose will be titrated, so the plan is visible at rounds.\n- **Route a dose above 200 mg through pharmacy and the attending.** If there is a clinical reason I don't know about, they can review it and place the order directly. They are better placed to check the indication and monitoring.\n\nIf you want a standard dose, tell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
      }
